  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =11+\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =11 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =\\frac{11}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{4}{11}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(\\frac{4}{11})=(19.983\\,1\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248{19.983}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${19.983}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={19.983}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{\u2218}+x={180}^{\u2218}+{19.983}^{\u2218}={199.983}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n19.983\\cdot 199.983\u22483\\,996\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
